    "media:imagetext": "NORTHWEST ORIENT\nCOMPLETE SYSTEM TIMETABLE\nGeneral Schedule C.A.B. No. 71, C.T.C. (A) (GS) No. 59\nEFFECTIVE APRIL 25, 1982\nSchedule Information\nPages 2-3\nDomestic Schedules\nPages 4-19\nAtlantic Passenger Schedules\nPage 20\nPacific Passenger Schedules\nPage 21\nAll-Cargo Schedules\nPage 22\nSummary of Changes\nPage 23\nIndex of Flights\nPage 24\nAIRCRAFT OPERATED:\nBoeing 747, Douglas DC10\nBoeing 727S, Boeing 727\nCLASS OF SERVICE:\n-First Clas\n• -Coach/International Econom\nFN-Deluxe Night Coach-\nFirst Class Compartment\nYN-Night Coach-\nCoach Compartment\n• -Midway Coono\n-Midway Economy\nISSUED:\nMarch 23, 1982\nEXPLANATION OF REFERENCES\nAEAL SERVICE: B- Breakfast: H- Brunch: L- Lunch: D- Dinner; S- Snack; F\nakfast in first\n- Lunch in first clas\nsnack in coach\nencircled indicate\nnational paste at normal med fimesntary meal service is provided on all inter-\nFOOTNOTES:\nawa or Osaka\nAlso, no local trattic permitted on\n47F aircraf\nHong\nOsaka or Tokyo;\nand\nLondon.\nStop over fratric permited between\ntockholm\nShannon and\nGlasgow.\nNo local\nStoDover Tronic Derween London and The Tollowing\nHamburg, Shannon, Glasgow, Stockholm.\nISSUED BY: ALLAN K. PRAY, Director, Schedule Planning\nNORTHWEST AIRLINES, INC.\nMinneapolis-Saint Paul International Airport\narrival of the Mobile Lounge at terminal.\nDulles International Airport is departure or\nSCHEDULE TIMES:\nsubtract 12\nimes are Local Times observed by each city. EST-Eastern Standard, EDT\ncastern Advance.\nCST-Central Standard\nco-entral\nHavanCe\nMST-\nMountain Standard. MDT-Mountain Advance. PST-Pacific Standard. PDT-\nPacific Advance, AST-Alaska Standard, ADT-Alaska Advance, HST-Hawaii\nEFFECTIVE:\nApril 25, 1982\n(EXCEPT AS NOTED)",
